  "scope": "C/Rust debug and plain q35/KVM SMP2 kernels each pass57 combined (48core+9BRD), then48 isolated core. All14 completion,10 swait and21 generic wait definitions selected exactly once; scheduler-text placement retained.",
  "diagnostics": "No compiler/objtool or rejected runtime diagnostics and no required skips. Debug instrumentation and plain exclusions resolve exactly; BUG=y in both.",
  "new_coverage": "Four WOKEN cases cover a prelatched running callback, zero/positive timeouts, blocked condition/payload handoff and bit-key address/bit matching while ignoring timeout. Entries remain linked until explicit removal. Scheduler samples establish descheduling at observation; finite tests do not prove universal ordering.",
  "remaining_C": "Entry initialization, default callback, bit-wait and locked interruptible policies, mixed flags/barrier operations, spinlock/lockdep/list/state adapters, scheduler and macros.",
  "limitations": "No universal barrier/race proof, stop/park, socket/futex consumer integration, blocked wait-bit policy, POLLFREE race, CFI/modules/arm64/performance proof. Concurrent WOKEN relatching is allowed; strict final-clear assertions only cover isolated cases.",
